{
  "about": "Meshpool Auto: which agent gets a new task. Each category lists keywords and, per agent, a benchmark quality score from 0 to 100 (the solve rate where measured) and, where measured, cost_usd and seconds per solved task. Auto takes the best quality among the agents that are installed and signed in, treats every agent within quality_band points of it as equally good, and among those picks the cheapest, then the fastest. The source field says where each number came from.",
  "version": 4,
  "source": "docs/BENCHMARKS.md. code (v4, 20 Nov 2026): the 52-task V2 eval on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, one run each (docs/results/v3/EVAL52_FINAL.md, CODEX_ENGINE_EVAL.md): Meshpool Code with the 0.0.7 Codex-design engine 47/52 $0.0034/task 19 s median, Pi 48/52, Hermes 49/52 (46.6 s), Codex 50/52 and 47/52 on a rerun (score 93 is their mean): all a tie within run-to-run noise (+/-3 tasks). Cost and time: Meshpool Code $0.0038 per solved task and 19 s from CODEX_ENGINE_EVAL; Pi, Hermes and Codex from the earlier EVAL52_FINAL batch, so these are from different batches and not a head-to-head; against Codex, run the same day, cost and time also tie (0.94x and 1.10x, intervals include 1). Auto therefore picks Meshpool Code on a tie, not on a measured win. The 13 Nov SWE-bench numbers were for the engine before 0.0.7. research and gtm (v4): no measurement for any agent, so Meshpool Work (the bundled browser and web research tools, twice as fast as Hermes on the eval) is set above Hermes, which only Meshpool Work gets a Chat bonus over. terminal: Terminal-Bench 2.0 run C, 15 tasks (Codex 8/15 $0.060, Meshpool loop 6/15 $0.182). browser: MiniWoB++ run C, 102 runs, for quality (Meshpool loop 97/102) and the 12 Nov dev round, 10 tasks at the same time, for cost and time (Meshpool loop $0.0009 18.7 s, Pi $0.0014 22.5 s, Codex $0.0025 23.3 s). Every other score is an estimate set below the measured agents; Hermes and the office categories have no cost or time yet.",
